From fbdc154a59a4fa843f4742a901ea6a20e5ccaac0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Oct 2024 19:42:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: fix shutdown in peripheral mode when gadget isn't
 configured

When in peripheral mode, the low level HW may have been left disabled
from the probe, e.g.:
	/* Gadget code manages lowlevel hw on its own */
	if (hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL)
		dwc2_lowlevel_hw_disable(hsotg);

It can be the case when no gadget configuration has been applied.
It could happen if the gadget has been removed before suspending.

When going to shutdown, register access in dwc2_is_device_mode(dwc2) will
trigger an exception:

E/TC:0   stm32_serc_handle_ilac:133 SERC exceptions [191:160]: 0x2000000
E/TC:0   stm32_serc_handle_ilac:139 SERC exception ID: 185
[   99.262259] Internal error: synchronous external abort: 0000000096000210 [#1] PREEMPT SMP
[   99.264829] Modules linked in:
